SUMMARY:Kokedama
LOCATION:181 Fremont - Level 39, Residents’ Club
DESCRIPTION:The Japanese art of moss ball gardening. You’ll wrap a living plant in nutrient-rich soil and soft moss to make a kokedama, a sculptural piece that sits on a shelf or hangs by a window.
